[{:db/id 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8116a58f-3c71-50dd-834a-34d7c8e130b8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-37e33b7e-4ee9-510a-871b-336b8d3b6afc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-257a594e-f07f-5439-bc42-9479c53748a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8116a58f-3c71-50dd-834a-34d7c8e130b8" :question/id #uuid "8116a58f-3c71-50dd-834a-34d7c8e130b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-70482" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a9278747563bf79a79e5633f2fae6d97a6ba021c38e8238ef9d22d1396df0be6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68bda977-95ea-5290-8305-157e4a10e1b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68bda977-95ea-5290-8305-157e4a10e1b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "68bda977-95ea-5290-8305-157e4a10e1b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-442cd84d-41ff-5be9-a617-0975ae88405b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-442cd84d-41ff-5be9-a617-0975ae88405b" "answer-bb8a8e9f-72f4-5ce4-95d3-47d890d2d058" "answer-940a5b9f-f125-53e4-989b-e5108b954ad8" "answer-697185c8-8a32-538c-a5da-d37c0206b23f" "answer-67c9df9f-085a-5a77-b0da-da891883eb22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-442cd84d-41ff-5be9-a617-0975ae88405b" :answer/id #uuid "442cd84d-41ff-5be9-a617-0975ae88405b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb8a8e9f-72f4-5ce4-95d3-47d890d2d058" :answer/id #uuid "bb8a8e9f-72f4-5ce4-95d3-47d890d2d058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-940a5b9f-f125-53e4-989b-e5108b954ad8" :answer/id #uuid "940a5b9f-f125-53e4-989b-e5108b954ad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-697185c8-8a32-538c-a5da-d37c0206b23f" :answer/id #uuid "697185c8-8a32-538c-a5da-d37c0206b23f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67c9df9f-085a-5a77-b0da-da891883eb22" :answer/id #uuid "67c9df9f-085a-5a77-b0da-da891883eb22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37e33b7e-4ee9-510a-871b-336b8d3b6afc" :question/id #uuid "37e33b7e-4ee9-510a-871b-336b8d3b6afc" :question/math-academy-id "q-16551" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0faaa905476ef6b6224a4b6b24ceb1adde4b14680507a7c6289885dce1bdd997.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9fa936b-ac16-50be-bf66-4d709c62af39"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9fa936b-ac16-50be-bf66-4d709c62af39" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9fa936b-ac16-50be-bf66-4d709c62af39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f2f00129-bfef-5325-bde1-618b368cc3e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d0bb612-0c9d-520f-8d2d-1cd458c72942" "answer-f94ac654-4ebc-5c1d-bd20-dcd10dcce606" "answer-d3edf35a-4f87-5270-a7f9-9191deeedcf0" "answer-1a520ba4-1bc5-52a1-8b92-4fc8f8534ee4" "answer-f2f00129-bfef-5325-bde1-618b368cc3e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d0bb612-0c9d-520f-8d2d-1cd458c72942" :answer/id #uuid "9d0bb612-0c9d-520f-8d2d-1cd458c72942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f94ac654-4ebc-5c1d-bd20-dcd10dcce606" :answer/id #uuid "f94ac654-4ebc-5c1d-bd20-dcd10dcce606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3edf35a-4f87-5270-a7f9-9191deeedcf0" :answer/id #uuid "d3edf35a-4f87-5270-a7f9-9191deeedcf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a520ba4-1bc5-52a1-8b92-4fc8f8534ee4" :answer/id #uuid "1a520ba4-1bc5-52a1-8b92-4fc8f8534ee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{5}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2f00129-bfef-5325-bde1-618b368cc3e7" :answer/id #uuid "f2f00129-bfef-5325-bde1-618b368cc3e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answe